  "Developer": "gameXcore Studios",
  "Genres": "Puzzle",
  "Name": "Don't Fear The Sweeper",
  "Overview": "Don't Fear The Sweeper is a straight Minesweeper variant. There is a grid and each time the player clicks on a field, the game either ends (a hidden bomb was found) or a number is revealed. This number shows how many bombs are found in the direct vicinity. Using those hints, the player has to work out where the bombs are hidden. Flags are used to mark the bomb spots. The game successfully ends when all fields without bombs are revealed.\n\nThis variant features four difficulty levels and a high-score list based on the time required to clear the field.",
